WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.060
A paw pulls away from a touch.

2
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.400
Does that tell you how much it hurts?

3
00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:12.283
Every behavioural result so far was a withdrawal threshold.

4
00:00:13.163 --> 00:00:15.203
A reflex is easy to mistake for pain.

5
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:20.943
Corder and colleagues imaged neurons in the basolateral amygdala of male mice,

6
00:00:20.943 --> 00:00:22.583
across repeated sessions.

7
00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.327
One ensemble responded to noxious stimuli and encoded their unpleasantness.

8
00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:33.337
After a nerve injury, innocuous stimuli recruited the same ensemble.

9
00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:38.317
Then they tagged those neurons genetically, and silenced them.

10
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:43.867
Predict. With the ensemble silenced, does the paw still pull away?

11
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.500
Yes. The withdrawal reflexes were preserved.

12
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.660
But escape and avoidance fell.

13
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.380
The reflex and the affective behaviour are two measurements, and they can come

14
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.480
apart. This was male mice, in one model.

15
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.750
In people, these cell-type manipulations cannot be done.

16
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.690
So the human study here asks a different question: prediction.

17
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.760
Baliki and colleagues scanned adults whose back pain was still subacute.

18
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.700
A year later, they asked who still had pain.

19
00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:28.183
Recovering meant a set drop in pain intensity.

20
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:30.203
It did not mean pain-free.

21
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:36.503
Stronger baseline connectivity between medial prefrontal cortex and nucleus

22
00:01:36.503 --> 00:01:38.443
accumbens predicted who persisted.

23
00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:41.883
That area is a pair-ordering probability.

24
00:01:42.743 --> 00:01:45.223
It is not a cause, and not one person's risk.

25
00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:50.807
The takeaway: in rodent models, the wiring, the cord and the immune cells all

26
00:01:50.807 --> 00:01:55.387
change. In mice, affective behaviour can be separated from the reflex.

27
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.647
In people, we have association and prediction.
